# cap_g6_syscap_inventory.oot — SysCap residual bulk (CAP-G6 honesty)
# Date: 2026-08-12
# Role: inventory only — not a claim that SysCap migration is complete

## Decision

**Net + fs product facades** migrate to granular tokens this wave.
**SysCap residual bulk remains** — documented here so CAP-G6 can close net+fs
without greenwashing full std least-privilege.

## Counts (host tip, 2026-08-12)

| Surface | Token | Approx lines |
|---------|-------|--------------|
| `ooda/std` | `&SysCap` | **16** across 3 files |
| `std` (external monorepo) | `&SysCap` | **~578** lines |
| `std` | `&ProcessCap` | **0** |
| `std` | `&NetCap` | ~17 (post net wave residual) |
| `std` | `&HttpCap` | ~7 |
| `std` | `&FsReadCap` / `&FsWriteCap` | ~6 each |
| `std` | legacy `&FsCap` | ~6 residual |

## Product ooda/std — named residual files

| File | Why still SysCap |
|------|------------------|
| `std/os/process.oo` | `process_spawn` / `wait` / `kill` / `exec` still take `&SysCap`. CAP-G4 path-A **prefers** ProcessCap at sealed ops (`sys_exec` et al.) with SysCap supersede; **facade not yet ProcessCap**. Hard residual: `process_epoll_create` / `inotify_init` / `prctl` **must** stay SysCap (ProcessCap ↛ hard Sys). |
| `std/os/async.oo` | `spawn_task` / `join_task` → `async_spawn_internal` / join. Spawn path can accept ProcessCap at runtime (CAP-G4); **join is hard SysCap-only**. Facade still SysCap. |
| `std/os/python.oo` | `load_model` → `python_embed_internal` — **hard SysCap only** (CAP-G4 map). |

## External std — residual bulk by domain (top)

| Domain (under `std/src/ooda/`) | ~SysCap hits | Notes |
|-------------------------------|--------------|-------|
| `sec/crypto` | ~134 | HSM/PKCS, SPHINCS, zkstark stubs — SysCap as default-deny gate, not ProcessCap |
| `sec/sys` | ~105 | landlock/enclave/audit/CFI stubs — OS residual; often correctly SysCap |
| `auto` / `aero` | ~46 / ~38 | domain stubs |
| `sec/net` | ~37 | WAF/JWT/mTLS residual — some TcpCap migration this wave (mTLS session) |
| `crypto` | ~28 | keys/HSM hardware paths |
| `robot` / `edge` / `bio` / `quantum` / `grid` / `3d` / `gui` / … | remainder | comment + param stubs; many pure math already cap-free |

Top single files (illustrative): `hsm_pkcs.oo`, `edge/ota.oo`, audit/enclave/landlock stubs.

## What CAP-G6 net+fs wave does **not** claim

- Full std migration off SysCap / NetCap / FsCap
- ProcessCap facades for `process_spawn`/`exec` (next residual wave)
- HW/UI product sealed ops (CAP-G3 residual-only still holds)
- OS isolation / seccomp (CAP-G5 residual honesty)

## Next residual waves (not this close)

1. `ooda/std/os/process.oo` — spawn/wait/kill/exec → `&ProcessCap`; keep epoll/inotify/prctl on SysCap
2. `async.oo` — split spawn (ProcessCap) vs join (SysCap) honesty
3. Domain std SysCap stubs — only where a sealed op prefers ProcessCap; do not invent ProcessCap for pure stubs
4. Remaining NetCap call sites outside product facades (`std/src/net/dns` residual, etc.)

